 education, finance, culture, and research. Helsinki is 80 kilometres (50 mi) north of Tallinn, Estonia, 400 kilometres (250 mi) east of Stockholm, Sweden, and 300 kilometres (190 mi) west of Saint Petersburg, Russia. Helsinki is a bilingual municipality with Finnish and Swedish as its official languages.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Suomenlinna_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Suomenlinna_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helsinki"},"twins":["Q1085","Q656","Q226","Q472","Q585","Q1748","Q1754","Q1764","Q1899","Q10704","Q956","Q1770","Q64","Q9022","Q9832"]}